---Properties of a managed Cassandra cluster.
---@class azure.cosmos_db.ClusterResourceProperties
---@field provisioningState? azure.cosmos_db.ManagedCassandraProvisioningState The status of the resource at the time the operation was called.
---@field restoreFromBackupId? string To create an empty cluster, omit this field or set it to null. To restore a backup into a new cluster, set this field to the resource id of the backup.
---@field delegatedManagementSubnetId? string Resource id of a subnet that this cluster's management service should have its network interface attached to. The subnet must be routable to all subnets that will be delegated to data centers. The resource id must be of the form '/subscriptions/<subscription id>/resourceGroups/<resource group>/providers/Microsoft.Network/virtualNetworks/<virtual network>/subnets/<subnet>'
---@field cassandraVersion? string Which version of Cassandra should this cluster converge to running (e.g., 3.11). When updated, the cluster may take some time to migrate to the new version.
---@field clusterNameOverride? string If you need to set the clusterName property in cassandra.yaml to something besides the resource name of the cluster, set the value to use on this property.
---@field authenticationMethod? azure.cosmos_db.AuthenticationMethod Which authentication method Cassandra should use to authenticate clients. 'None' turns off authentication, so should not be used except in emergencies. 'Cassandra' is the default password based authentication. The default is 'Cassandra'.
---@field initialCassandraAdminPassword? distilled.Secret Initial password for clients connecting as admin to the cluster. Should be changed after cluster creation. Returns null on GET. This field only applies when the authenticationMethod field is 'Cassandra'.
---@field prometheusEndpoint? azure.cosmos_db.SeedNode Hostname or IP address where the Prometheus endpoint containing data about the managed Cassandra nodes can be reached.
---@field repairEnabled? boolean Should automatic repairs run on this cluster? If omitted, this is true, and should stay true unless you are running a hybrid cluster where you are already doing your own repairs.
---@field autoReplicate? azure.cosmos_db.AutoReplicate The form of AutoReplicate that is being used by this cluster.
---@field clientCertificates? azure.cosmos_db.ClusterResourcePropertiesClientCertificatesList List of TLS certificates used to authorize clients connecting to the cluster. All connections are TLS encrypted whether clientCertificates is set or not, but if clientCertificates is set, the managed Cassandra cluster will reject all connections not bearing a TLS client certificate that can be validated from one or more of the public certificates in this property.
---@field externalGossipCertificates? azure.cosmos_db.ClusterResourcePropertiesExternalGossipCertificatesList List of TLS certificates used to authorize gossip from unmanaged data centers. The TLS certificates of all nodes in unmanaged data centers must be verifiable using one of the certificates provided in this property.
---@field gossipCertificates? azure.cosmos_db.ClusterResourcePropertiesGossipCertificatesList List of TLS certificates that unmanaged nodes must trust for gossip with managed nodes. All managed nodes will present TLS client certificates that are verifiable using one of the certificates provided in this property.
---@field externalSeedNodes? azure.cosmos_db.ClusterResourcePropertiesExternalSeedNodesList List of IP addresses of seed nodes in unmanaged data centers. These will be added to the seed node lists of all managed nodes.
---@field seedNodes? azure.cosmos_db.ClusterResourcePropertiesSeedNodesList List of IP addresses of seed nodes in the managed data centers. These should be added to the seed node lists of all unmanaged nodes.
---@field externalDataCenters? azure.cosmos_db.ClusterResourcePropertiesExternalDataCentersList List of the data center names for unmanaged data centers in this cluster to be included in auto-replication.
---@field hoursBetweenBackups? number (Deprecated) Number of hours to wait between taking a backup of the cluster.
---@field deallocated? boolean Whether the cluster and associated data centers has been deallocated.
---@field cassandraAuditLoggingEnabled? boolean Whether Cassandra audit logging is enabled
---@field provisionError? azure.cosmos_db.CassandraError Error related to resource provisioning.
---@field extensions? azure.cosmos_db.ClusterResourcePropertiesExtensionsList Extensions to be added or updated on cluster.
---@field backupSchedules? azure.cosmos_db.ClusterResourcePropertiesBackupSchedulesList List of backup schedules that define when you want to back up your data.
---@field scheduledEventStrategy? azure.cosmos_db.ScheduledEventStrategy How the nodes in the cluster react to scheduled events
---@field azureConnectionMethod? azure.cosmos_db.AzureConnectionType How to connect to the azure services needed for running the cluster
---@field privateLinkResourceId? string If the Connection Method is Vpn, this is the Id of the private link resource that the datacenters need to connect to.

